# memory_gap_many_ranges: Guest RAM in thirteen ranges: the first, then twelve of one page each, physically adjacent, listed to the device in reverse order (the memory map sorts them). A child FIFO whose three ring pages are three of those ranges, with a command straddling each page boundary (the ring is one range mapping of three pieces); a depth-3 task whose task root and three tables are four more of them; and a buffer over the last five, one physical run across five ranges, filled from its first page to its last. In the map and isolate setups the fill lands in all five; in the blocks setup the host cannot map a range that crosses its ranges and the exec faults (as in memory_gap_ram_holes), while the child FIFO, whose pages the root task maps one range each, runs in every setup.
